          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4101,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 669443542,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "No, this definitely is not religious, just ensuring, that we do not duplicate functionality. I agree, that using this for C Plugins is a valid usecase.\n\nAs your intention is putting it into a plugin, if you enable this globally, it would slow down dissection even if you do not use the plugin otherwise except for it being present. My guess would be, that this needs to be added to the registration function for plugins, and therefore would be present throughout the code. Also, it could be prudent to mimic the methodology of the LUA engine and not make this method public, but rather change the registration method (like Listener.new) to enable deeper dissection if required. This might be even less intrusive as it might just apply (would need a deeper look at the registration function) to the single dissection when the plugin would be called anyways.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
